hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27750","Haddathana Husayn ibn Muhammad and Surayj ibn al-Numan who said: Haddathana Khalaf from Abu Malik al-Ashjai from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me."
"27751","Haddathana Husayn ibn Muhammad: Haddathana Khalaf from Abu Malik who said: My father had prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sixteen years old, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman; so I said to him: Did they recite qunut; he said: No, my son, it is innovated."
"27752","[Truncated in source: Haddathana only, no matn transmitted]."
"27753","Haddathana Yazid who said: Haddathana Abu Malik who said: Haddathani my father that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when a person came to him asking him, he said: O Prophet of Allah, how shall I say when I ask my Lord; he said: Say: O Allah, forgive me and have mercy on me and guide me and provide for me; and he closed his fist except the thumb and said: These gather for you the good of your world and your hereafter."
"27754","He said: And I heard him say to the people: Whoever unifies Allah and disbelieves in what is worshipped besides Him, his wealth and his blood are forbidden, and his reckoning is upon Allah, mighty and majestic."
"27755","Haddathana Ismail ibn Muhammad who said: Haddathana Marwan ibn Muawiya who said: Haddathana Abu Malik al-Ashjai who said: Haddathani my father who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever unifies Allah and disbelieves in what is worshipped besides Him, Allah has forbidden his wealth and his blood, and his reckoning is upon Allah, mighty and majestic."
